# AU-Tum TAM Parameter List - Version 2 Complete (All 17 TAM parameters, zero-GPP prevention)
# Based on empirical analysis of 1000-member ensemble (analyze_zero_gpp.py)
#
# CRITICAL FINDING: Original ensemble had 34.2% zero-GPP cases
# Root cause: Low root C:N + Long absorptive root longevity = N sequestration in roots
#
# This version keeps ALL original TAM parameters but adjusts ranges to avoid zero GPP
# Format: parameter_name distribution_type min max
# ==================================================================================

# ROOT C:N RATIOS (Transport, Absorptive, Mycorrhizal)
# CRITICAL: These are the most important parameters - 4-6% impact on GPP
# Low C:N (high N content) causes zero GPP by sequestering N in roots
# Analysis shows: froottcn needs >100, frootacn needs >70 to avoid zero GPP
froottcn 5 95 165    # Transport root C:N (was 20-184, min raised 20→95)
frootacn 5 65 115    # Absorptive root C:N (was 11-119, min raised 11→65)
frootmcn 5 12 23     # Mycorrhizal root C:N (was 7-25, narrowed for safety)

# ROOT C:P RATIOS (Transport, Absorptive, Mycorrhizal)
# NOTE: These show correlation with each other (expected for root functional types)
# Kept all three to preserve TAM framework, narrowed ranges slightly
froottcp 5 450 950   # Transport root C:P (was 375-1125, tightened)
frootacp 5 300 700   # Absorptive root C:P (was 250-750, tightened)
frootmcp 5 100 1400  # Mycorrhizal root C:P (was 10-1600, raised minimum)

# ROOT LONGEVITY (Transport, Absorptive, Mycorrhizal)
# CRITICAL: Long absorptive roots + high N = zero GPP
# Analysis shows: froota_long > 1.23 causes zero GPP (in combination with low C:N)
# Adjusted to safe range while maintaining TAM variation
froott_long 5 4.5 9  # Transport root longevity (years) (was 3-10, narrowed)
froota_long 5 0.7 1.3 # Absorptive root longevity (years) (was 0.5-4, max reduced 4→1.3)
frootm_long 5 0.25 0.8 # Mycorrhizal root longevity (years) (was 0.13-1, adjusted)

# ROOT CHEMISTRY - LABILE FRACTIONS (Transport, Absorptive, Mycorrhizal)
# Lower impact but kept for TAM completeness
# Tightened ranges to avoid extreme chemistry combinations
frt_flab 5 0.15 0.32  # Transport root labile fraction (was 0.1-0.35, narrowed)
frt_fcel 5 0.38 0.62  # Transport root cellulose fraction (was 0.35-0.65, narrowed)
fra_flab 5 0.15 0.32  # Absorptive root labile fraction (was 0.1-0.35, narrowed)
fra_fcel 5 0.38 0.62  # Absorptive root cellulose fraction (was 0.35-0.65, narrowed)
frm_flab 5 0.15 0.32  # Mycorrhizal root labile fraction (was 0.1-0.35, narrowed)
frm_fcel 5 0.38 0.62  # Mycorrhizal root cellulose fraction (was 0.35-0.65, narrowed)

# ROOT-LEAF ALLOCATION (Transport, Absorptive)
# Controls carbon partitioning to leaves - important for GPP
# Avoid very low values that would limit leaf allocation
froott_leaf 5 0.12 0.35  # Transport root to leaf allocation (was 0.05-0.4, raised min)
froota_leaf 5 0.25 0.55  # Absorptive root to leaf allocation (was 0.2-0.6, slightly adjusted)

# ==================================================================================
# PARAMETER COUNT: 17 (ALL original TAM parameters preserved)
#
# ZERO GPP PREVENTION STRATEGY:
#   Original ensemble: 342/1000 (34.2%) produced zero GPP
#   Root cause identified: Low root C:N + Long absorptive roots = N sequestration
#
#   Key adjustments to prevent zero GPP:
#   1. froottcn min:    20 → 95  (avoid N-luxury transport roots)
#   2. frootacn min:    11 → 65  (avoid N-luxury absorptive roots)
#   3. froota_long max:  4 → 1.3 (avoid long-lived N-rich absorptive roots)
#   4. froott_leaf min: 0.05 → 0.12 (ensure minimum leaf allocation)
#
#   Expected result: <5% zero GPP cases (down from 34.2%)
#
# PARAMETER CORRELATION NOTES:
#   - CN ratios for T/A/M roots show some correlation (biologically expected)
#   - CP ratios show correlation (biologically expected)
#   - This is acceptable - TAM framework depends on root type differentiation
#   - Use informative priors in MCMC to handle correlation
#
# BIOLOGICAL CONSTRAINTS RESPECTED:
#   - Transport roots: Long-lived, low N, high lignin
#   - Absorptive roots: Short-lived, high N, low lignin
#   - Mycorrhizal associations: Variable chemistry, moderate longevity
#
# CALIBRATION RECOMMENDATIONS:
#   - Ensemble size: 1000 samples minimum (17 parameters × 60 samples/param)
#   - Target surrogate R²: >0.90 for GPP, ER, NPP; >0.85 for NEE
#   - Dynamic range: Should cover 2500-4500 gC/m²/year for GPP
#
# WARNING:
#   This TAM-only configuration (no leaf parameters) may have limited GPP range
#   If surrogates show insufficient range after 1000-member ensemble:
#     → Consider adding leafcn, slatop to expand dynamic range
#     → See AU-Tum_parm_list_tam_v2_robust for version with leaf parameters
#
# VALIDATION:
#   After running ensemble, validate with: check_AUTum_surrogate_robustness.py
#   If zero GPP persists, use: analyze_zero_gpp.py for further diagnosis
